\section{Use Effect Tokens to Bound Cross-Block Motion}

An address being available at the insertion point does not prove
that it will yield the same value there. Consider hoisting a read out
of a successor reached by a branch. Assume the read is ordinary,
nonvolatile, proved safe to execute at the insertion point, and from
memory that cannot change asynchronously. Use memory SSA with one
token for the read's alias class. Tokens here identify reaching
memory definitions, not executable values. For simplicity require
exact token equality and an insertion point that dominates the
original read; leave side-entry repair and alias-based relaxations to
other passes. Also preserve ordering against any separately modeled
observable effects.

\begin{sudocode}[Conservative memory-motion gate]
\If{$p$ does not dominate the original read point $q$}
  \State \Return keep at $q$ \Comment{All users need a definition}
\EndIf
\If{address unavailable or read not safe at $p$}
  \State \Return keep at $q$
\EndIf
\State $k\gets$ alias class of the read
\If{$memory(k,p)\ne memory(k,q)$}
  \State \Return keep at $q$ \Comment{An old token is not a value proof}
\EndIf
\If{other ordering obligations permit the move}
  \State \Return place at $p$
\EndIf
\State \Return keep at $q$
\end{sudocode}

Let address $a$ initially hold 3. Point $p$ is before an unconditional
store of 8 to $a$; after the store the branch enters a block that reads
$a$ and returns it. The other arm returns 0. The tokens differ, so the
read stays in place and the two outputs are 8 and 0. Moving it would
produce 3 on the read arm. Now redirect the store to $b$ in a proven
disjoint alias class: the tokens for $a$ agree, and the hoisted read
returns 3 on the selected arm without adding an observation on the other.

The invariant is that every path that originally read observes the same
memory version, while paths that did not read gain only a harmless
speculative operation. A memory phi whose operands ultimately represent
the same version may still fail exact-identity comparison. That loses
an opportunity, not correctness. Pressure and path probability should
be consulted only after this legality check.
